<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30223" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mȳlae</span></b> , ārum (and
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mȳlē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., <i><span class="en">Sil. 14,
		202</span></i>), f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μύλαι</span>.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A city in Sicily</i>, now <i>Milazzo</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 8, 14, § 90</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 2,
				79, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 16</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mȳlaeus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Mylæ, Mylæan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aut Pompeiani Mylaea pericula belli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Mosell. 215</span></i>
			 (al. Milasena).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A city in Thessaly</i>, now <i>Dhamasi</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 42, 54</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Two islands near Crete</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12,
				20, § 61</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
